## WHAT THIS LANE IS (RELAYED from PCOMP-95 and gate B626; verify each at source yourself)
Jira PCOMP-95, status Backlog, created 2026-10-25 11:22 (MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER: `project = PCOMP AND ( key = PCOMP-95 )` returns exactly 1 issue; `project = PCOMP AND ( text ~ "B626" )` returns exactly that same 1 issue; read whole). PR #88 (squash `cece687e199b6d84e82151b3c36127fa4a6b31b2`, merged 2026-10-25 09:55 AEDT, NOT deployed) refuses a date in year 0000 with 400 INVALID_REQUEST. Gate B626 found **no product defect** (every malformed or leap-year date it forced through the API got the correct refusal) and **three Major test gaps** (G-6: a surviving mutant on the date rule). Source of the rule: `apps/api/src/app.ts` at main (blob sha `2c5d5ad1`, equal to the gate's head blob: MEASURED-BY-DRAFTER by `gh api contents`): `:105` `const DATE = /^(\d{4})-(\d{2})-(\d{2})$/;`, `:118-120` `Number(match[n])`, `:124` the `leapYear` constant, `:125` `return day <= (month === 2 && leapYear ? 29 : (DAYS_IN_MONTH[month - 1] ?? 0));`, `:157-159` `onCreate: (ajv) => { ajv.addFormat("date", isStorableDate); }`.

**THE 15 ROWS (the gate's fix-shape: a shape, not a final row set; a value may differ only if you PROVE the replacement red against the same named mutant, in STATUS):**
| Finding | Rows | Route and field | Expected | Killed mutant(s) (each row must be RED under the one named for it, direct, not by knock-on) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| B626-1 (leap-year month lengths) | `"2024-02-30"`, `"2000-02-30"` | `updateEngagement` `due_date` | 400 INVALID_REQUEST, nothing stored | G01 (leap February gets 30 days: `leapYear ? 29 :` becomes `leapYear ? 30 :`) |
| B626-1 | `"2024-01-31"`, `"2024-03-31"`, `"2024-04-30"` | same | accepted (status below 300), and the stored value read back equals what was sent | G02 (leap test applied to every month: `month === 2 && leapYear ? 29` becomes `leapYear ? 29`) |
| B626-2 (a non-digit in a digit position of the right length) | `"abcd-01-01"`, `"1e03-01-01"`, `"+027-01-01"`, `" 027-01-01"` (leading space) | same | 400 INVALID_REQUEST, nothing stored | G05 (year group `(\d{4})` becomes `([\w\W]{4})`) |
| B626-2 | `"2027- 1-01"`, `"2027-+1-01"` | same | same | G06 (month group `(\d{2})` becomes `([\w\W]{2})`) |
| B626-2 | `"2027-01- 1"`, `"2027-01-1 "` (trailing space), `"2027-01-+1"` | same | same | G07 (day group becomes `([\w\W]{2})`) |
| B626-3 (the registration) | `expires_at` `"2027-01-01T00:00:00Z"` accepted (201, the stored `expires_at` read back is that instant); in the same row or a second one the bare `"2027-01-01"` answers 400 INVALID_REQUEST | `createMembership` (as the harness's platform administrator, as the existing `s44-fx-id.db.test.ts` rows at `:769-797` call it: `POST /memberships`, `as: "platform-admin"`, body `{ tenant_id, user_id, role, expires_at }`) | as stated | N18 (`ajv.addFormat("date-time", isStorableDate);` added after the `date` line) |
Count: 5 + 9 + 1 = **15** (14 on `updateEngagement` `due_date`, one on `createMembership` `expires_at`). **One `it` per value** (a loop of `it`s, as the existing file does), so each is red BY NAME under its mutant. You may add up to three further control rows (for example an accepted ordinary `expires_at` of `null`, or a non-leap `"2027-02-29"` that stays refused); each is stated BEFORE the first run, with the mutant that turns it red or the words "control, green by design".

**The facts the rows rest on (RELAYED from the gate; you re-measure each one you quote):** the gate's oracle: G01 accepts 2,424 strings (YYYY-02-30 for every leap year) and PostgreSQL refuses each (SQLSTATE 22008), so the head would answer **500** to `"2024-02-30"`; G02 refuses 43,632 storable dates; G05/G06/G07 let malformed strings answer **500** or be **stored** (`" 027-01-01"` is stored as `0027-01-01`, `"2027-01-1 "` as `2027-01-01`); under N18 the two valid date-times answer **400** and the bare date answers **201**. At main every row's expected answer is the head's (the gate forced each value through the route: B626 STATUS lines 19-41). The PR's runtime behaviour is correct today: **all 15 rows are GREEN on main by design**; their red proof is the six mutants, which live only in `wt-b671-mut`.

